    <!-- "teh" is the README's deliberate misspelling example. -->
    <string name="cleanup_dictionary_help" tools:ignore="Typos">Each rule turns a word or phrase the app keeps getting wrong into what you meant.\n\n• Matches whole words in any case: “teh” matches “Teh” but not “tehran”.\n• In Chinese and Japanese, which have no spaces between words, a phrase also matches inside a sentence. In Korean it also matches with a particle attached: “메일” matches “메일을”.\n• A capital letter on the right side is kept as written. Otherwise the case follows what was heard: “Teh” becomes “The”.\n• Leave the right side empty to delete the phrase.\n• When rules overlap, the longest match wins.</string>
    <string name="cleanup_dictionary_empty">No rules yet. Tap “Add rule” to fix a word the app keeps getting wrong.</string>
    <string name="cleanup_dictionary_add">Add rule</string>
    <string name="cleanup_dictionary_edit">Edit rule</string>
