    <string name="onboarding_keyboard_warning">Android warns that any keyboard you turn on could collect what you type. That warning is standard. Marmalade STT only types what you dictate, and nothing leaves your phone.</string>
    <!-- The Pixel's second dialog: the keyboard isn't direct-boot aware (models live in credential-encrypted storage). -->
    <string name="onboarding_keyboard_unlock_note">Some phones then show a second message: after a reboot, the app can\'t start until you unlock your phone. That\'s fine too. Tap OK.</string>
